# R6-2 (1) (steps/receiver-routes-census-20261010.md, cluster 4; Codex CODEX-R6-SCOPE-20261011-102505): a merge result
# body is read by the common Structure body construction -- the same items, the same check, the same schema -- so it
# holds what a named Structure's body holds: beside the typed field w, a nested Structure Inner with its own field v and
# an Array xs of two ints, each built by the unit as a named Structure's is and copied by the merge as any operand's
# children are.  Each reads back through the result.  Exit 7; 81/82/83/84 name the field that came back wrong.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model

R: merge: Model
    int: w 4
    Inner:
        int: v 3
    end: Inner
    []: int xs 2
end: merge
int: w R\w
int: v R\Inner\v
size_t: n length(R\xs)
size_t: x R\x
if: w != 4
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: v != 3
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 82; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: n != 2U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 83; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
if: x != 1U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 84; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
